Route marlin_gemm through the locally built tunable Marlin extension.

VLLM_MARLIN_TUNE=1 loads ~/marlin-tune/src (the standalone build of this same
vLLM 0.27.1 Marlin source with a runtime (size_n, size_k, key, m_max) -> tile
config table resolved inside marlin_mm) and routes ops.marlin_gemm through it.
CUDA graphs and torch.compile see a single custom op either way — the load is
EAGER at import because an import/set_table inside the wrapper would land
inside dynamo tracing and graph-break the boot.

Two row families share the table (marlin_best.py):
  - fp16-activation decode rows (m_max<=16): the M<=8/16 verify GEMMs,
    +3-7% per GEMM on sm86.
  - int8-activation prefill rows, keyed 100+weight_bits and only consulted at
    M>=1024 (the C++ lookup maps a_bits==8 onto that key), so decode GEMMs can
    never match them: chunked-prefill W4A8 GEMMs at M=2048, where stock's tile
    heuristic leaves 2-20% per GEMM on the table (gate_up: >+20%).

The fake-tensor impl mirrors stock's dtype rule (int8/fp8 activations produce
scale-dtype output), without which torch.compile traces the wrong dtype on the
W4A8 path.

No-op without the extension: a failed import logs and falls back to stock.
Build the extension per ~/marlin-tune/src/build.sh (CUDA 13 pip toolchain);
install its path as a .pth in the venv (echo .../marlin-tune/src > site-packages/marlin_tune.pth).

Apply from the installed vllm package directory:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/0023-marlin-tune-table.patch

Written against vLLM 0.27.1.

--- a/_custom_ops.py
